IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Water Industry Act 1991 (UK) — WORKING DAYS (s 144(7)).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1991-56.txt.

§ `Working days`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- The Gregorian computus (Meeus, Jones and Butcher) for Easter Sunday.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Easter Sunday in` y MEANS
    Date (((h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114) MODULO 31) PLUS 1) (FLOOR ((h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114) DIVIDED BY 31)) y
    WHERE
        a MEANS y MODULO 19
        b MEANS FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 100)
        c MEANS y MODULO 100
        d MEANS FLOOR (b DIVIDED BY 4)
        e MEANS b MODULO 4
        f MEANS FLOOR ((b PLUS 8) DIVIDED BY 25)
        g MEANS FLOOR ((b MINUS f PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3)
        h MEANS ((19 TIMES a) PLUS b MINUS d MINUS g PLUS 15) MODULO 30
        i MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 4)
        k MEANS c MODULO 4
        l MEANS (32 PLUS (2 TIMES e) PLUS (2 TIMES i) MINUS h MINUS k) MODULO 7
        m MEANS FLOOR ((a PLUS (11 TIMES h) PLUS (22 TIMES l)) DIVIDED BY 451)

-- s 144(7): "two working days" is "a period of forty-eight hours calculated
-- after disregarding any time falling on— (a) a Saturday or Sunday; or (b)
-- Christmas Day, Good Friday or any day which is a bank holiday in England
-- and Wales under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971." The bank
-- holidays are an input.
@ref s 144(7)
@export Whether a day counts towards "two working days" under s 144(7) of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK): not a Saturday, a Sunday, Christmas Day, Good Friday, or a bank holiday in England and Wales (given as a list). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A DATE              @desc The day
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE  @desc The bank holidays in England and Wales under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a working day` d `, bank holidays` holidays IF
        NOT (w EQUALS 6)
    AND NOT (w EQUALS 0)
    AND NOT (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 25)
    AND NOT (d EQUALS `the day` (0 MINUS 2) `days after` (`Easter Sunday in` (DATE_YEAR d)))
    AND NOT (elem d holidays)
    WHERE
        w MEANS `Weekday of` d

-- The n-th working day after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE, holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the` n `th working day after` d `, bank holidays` holidays MEANS
    IF   n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE IF   `is a working day` next `, bank holidays` holidays
         THEN `the` (n MINUS 1) `th working day after` next `, bank holidays` holidays
         ELSE `the` n `th working day after` next `, bank holidays` holidays
    WHERE
        next MEANS `the day` 1 `days after` d

